=begin pod :page-card<Troupes> :nav-order<50>

=TITLE Outreach Troupe

=head1 Purpose

The purpose of the Outreach troupe is to ensure the future of Raku by:

=item1 Ensure we have new people flowing into the community (Product 
Strategy/Marketing)

=item Ensuring it is easy for new members of the Raku community to enter the 
community and find their way to the places where they best serve either 
themselves and/or the community (depending on their interests).  

=item Enable Sharing: Making it easy for people to share Raku with their 
colleagues, associates, friends, and other people in their life.  

=item Social Cohesion activities

=head1 Activities

=head2 Ensure we have new people flowing into the community

=head3 Product Strategy

=item Product Vision
=item Target Audience
=item Market Analysis
=item Value Proposition
=item Key Initiatives
=item Success Metrics

=head2 Ensuring it's easy for new people to enter the community

=head3 The Entry Pathway

Look after raku.org to ensure that it's a good front door for newcomers.  
This includes pathway analysis on raku.org starting with a survey of 
404 errors, to see if any need to be replaced with 3xx responses that
send the viewer somewhere useful

=head3 Volunteer Relations/Social Media

=item Issue Weekly, cross-post to Reddit

=item Keep YouTube playlists up-to-date

=head2 Enable Sharing

Update marketing.raku.org

=head1 Resources

=head2 Code Repositories

=head2 IRC/Discord channels

For information about the IRC channels, see the L<#raku IRC channel|https://raku.org/community/irc/> page.  

=head2 Other communication

=head1 Projects

=head2 raku.org

=head2 marketing.raku.org

L<marketing.raku.org|https://marketing.raku.org> needs a serious update.  It's 
still all about Perl6.  

=item Flyers: These essentially just need an update to say "Raku" instead of 
Perl 6.  

=item Brochures: The "Introducing Perl 6" one could do with an update.  The 
other could be moved to an "Historical" section.  

=item Teasers: These should also be moved to an "Historical" section

=item Cards: Should be updated

=item Logos: These are up-to-date

We should also make it possible to buy physical copies (could the proceeds go to 
Raku?).  

Possibly we should also look at adopting the following:

=item L<Periodic table of Raku operators|https://www.ozonehouse.com/mark/periodic/>

=item L<Raku Cheat Sheet|https://github.com/perl6/mu/raw/master/docs/Perl6/Cheatsheet/cheatsheet.txt>

Note also the following:

=item L<Zazzle Raku/Rakudo Merch|https://www.zazzle.com/store/rakudo>

=item The following no longer functions usefully: L<Spreadshirt|https://www.spreadshirt.com/shop/rakudo/>

=head2 YouTube Playlist

These are terribly out-of-date (Perl 6, rather than Raku, and 7 years out of 
date), and will require updating before they can again be used in the 
documentation/outreach materials.  The current playlists are:

=item L<Perl 6 (English)|https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLRuESFRW2Fa77XObvk7-BYVFwobZHdXdK>

=item L<Perl 6 (Non-English)|https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLRuESFRW2Fa6PBxZ8oQhKqV8zZak3bHNN>

See also L<Create a curated YouTube Playlist|https://github.com/Raku/raku.org/issues/210>

=head3 The Medium Term

It'd be useful to have these updated, and broken into lists of 30-50 items, 
broken down by topic to a certain extent.  For example, there should probably be 
a "Web Development in Raku" list.  

Also, the non-English ones should be broken down by language in cases where 
there's more than one video in the language.  

=head3 The Long Term

Ideally what we'd replace them with is an integration with the Raku 
documentation (particularly the tutorials), and/or elucid8 (so that the same 
tech can be used in other raku-related sites).  There should be a way to tag the 
videos (key-value tags) so that they can be associated with particular documents 
in a useful way.  Or people can choose to watch by topic, author, or whatever.  

